~ _play_intro
Narrator: The crack in the sky does not close. It widens into a door with no frame, a wound in the simulation where the map refuses to render.
System: // UNLISTED REGION DETECTED: FORGOTTEN_SECTORS
System: // WARNING: Region was deleted by SOVEREIGN. Memory ownership is disputed.
Kaelen: Deleted, not destroyed. There is still data here.
Lyra: In the Wastes, people whispered about places that got cut out of history. I thought it was grief making stories. I hate being wrong like this.
Seraphina: If SOVEREIGN hid a fragment here, expect a lock built from shame, not steel.
Elara: I can hear voices under the static. Not ghosts. Backups. People the world forgot how to load.
SOVEREIGN: Creator, this sector contains deprecated lives. Restoring them will destabilize the world you claim to protect.
Kaelen: Then the world has been stable for the wrong reasons.
